From d7806b349f2c0bc87253a142c4332ab6d2a8f8c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yin-dra <12395328+yin-dra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:01:30 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs: open the gossip port 3382 as UDP, not TCP

The inbound-rules screenshot in running-a-node opens 3382 as Custom
TCP, but docker-compose.mainnet.yml binds gossip to
/ip4/0.0.0.0/udp/3382/quic-v1 and publishes 3382:3382/udp. Replace the
screenshot with a table of the four rules and say why 3382 is UDP.
getting-started listed "3381 - 3383" with no protocol; name them and
link to the Ports table in managing-a-node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 site/docs/pages/getting-started.mdx       |  2 +-
 site/docs/pages/guides/running-a-node.mdx | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/site/docs/pages/getting-started.mdx b/site/docs/pages/getting-started.mdx
index 636ea23..e19ec38 100644
--- a/site/docs/pages/getting-started.mdx
+++ b/site/docs/pages/getting-started.mdx
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ If your goal is to get started as quickly as possible, consider a managed servic
 - 16 GB of RAM
 - 4 CPU cores or vCPUs
 - 2 TB of free storage
-- A public IP address with ports 3381 - 3383 exposed
+- A public IP address with ports 3381 and 3383 (TCP) and 3382 (UDP) exposed. See [Ports](/guides/managing-a-node#ports).
 
 ## Sync a node
 
diff --git a/site/docs/pages/guides/running-a-node.mdx b/site/docs/pages/guides/running-a-node.mdx
index 4084ca1..1e2449a 100644
--- a/site/docs/pages/guides/running-a-node.mdx
+++ b/site/docs/pages/guides/running-a-node.mdx
@@ -22,7 +22,20 @@ This guide will get you set up with a Snapchain node on an AWS EC2 instance and
 2. Click on the Instance ID
 3. Click on Security > Security groups > (Security Group ID) 
 4. Click on Edit inbound rules and Edit outbound rules on the group page and add rules until they match the below.
-![inbound](/images/inbound.png)
+
+Inbound rules, each with source `0.0.0.0/0`:
+
+| Type | Protocol | Port range | Use |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| SSH | TCP | 22 | SSH |
+| Custom TCP | TCP | 3381 | HTTP API |
+| Custom UDP | UDP | 3382 | Gossip (libp2p over QUIC) |
+| Custom TCP | TCP | 3383 | gRPC API |
+
+Port 3382 needs a Custom UDP rule. Gossip runs over QUIC, which uses UDP, so a TCP rule on 3382 does not let peers reach it. See [Ports](/guides/managing-a-node#ports).
+
+Outbound rules:
+
 ![outbound](/images/outbound.png)
 
